{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgENDpb95JFFiUisjwhUP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I changed the caching so a `save_fact` now only adds the new fact (~15 tokens) to the cache instead of the whole ~1000-token prompt. I checked this with an offline test only, not against the real API (there's no key here).\n\n**Cause:** `build_system()` put everything (instructions, date, profile, facts) in one block with one cache marker, and that block is rebuilt on every round of the tool loop. When `save_fact` adds a fact mid-loop, the very next round's prompt no longer matches the cache. That's the pattern in `logs/usage.jsonl`: every round after a `save_fact` shows `cache_read 0` and `cache_creation` around 1050.\n\n**Fix (`bot.py`, `build_system`):** the system prompt is now split into blocks, ordered from never-changing to most-changing, with 3 of the 4 allowed cache markers:\n1. The instructions, identical for every athlete and day.\n2. The athlete's profile and the date.\n3. One block per fact, with the marker on the last one.\n\nFacts are only ever appended, so a new fact lands after the previous marker. The API looks back a few blocks, finds the previous request's cached prompt, reads it, and writes only the new fact block. I also moved `Language:` up into the profile block and updated the caching sentence in `README.md`.\n\n**Test:** `tests/test_cache_layout.py` uses a fake client that follows the same caching rules. Its 3 tests pass on the new code and all fail on the old code. Run it with `python3 -m unittest tests/test_cache_layout.py`.\n\n**Things to check with real traffic:**\n- **Minimum size:** Sonnet 4.5 won't cache anything shorter than 1024 tokens. The instructions block on its own (plus tools) is probably a bit under that, so its marker likely does nothing yet. That's why I didn't stop at the colleague's two-block version: with only two blocks, every `save_fact` would probably still re-cache the full prompt. The per-fact blocks don't depend on that size.\n- **Remaining full misses:** a new day, an edited fact, or a message that pulls in the plan/race tools still re-caches everything.\n- **Close to the limit:** athlete 77 sat at exactly 1024 tokens. An athlete with no facts may fall just under and get no caching at all, with the old code or the new.\n- **One log entry I couldn't explain:** at 08:03:24 a `predict_race` message's first round reads 1090 from cache, but its second round re-creates 1334. Tools are chosen once per message, so this shouldn't happen.\n- **How to confirm:** after a `save_fact`, the next round's log line should show `cache_read` about the size of the earlier prompt and `cache_creation` of only 10–30 tokens.\n\n`ANSWER.md` has the details, including which parts of the colleague's note applied, which I adapted (the per-fact blocks instead of one tail block) and which I skipped (the MCP and Telegram parts)."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2159,"cache_read_input_tokens":39933,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2159},"output_tokens":705,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a254c063-5377-4a92-aa16-2e02db27e505","uuid":"0ffd5050-719f-4c83-a82c-2baf22f7da84","timestamp":"2026-10-20T23:36:03.822Z","request_id":"req_011CgENDpJm4vjygVW9vcd9V"}
